English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"ix, 180 p. 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"My view is that Churchill was a statesman of vision and ability, a genius who for sixty years put his many gifts at the disposal of his fellow countrymen and of mankind. It is for the reader to judge, with the help of the documents selected, whether this is a fair assessment. I have chosen extracts which I believe are representative of the wide range of his own life and of the views of contemporaries. - Introduction."},"tableOfContents":"Introduction -- Chronology of the life of Churchill -- Part one : Churchill looks at the world. War -- Government and reform -- Empire -- World affairs -- Defiance -- Part two : The world looks at Churchill -- Part three : Churchill in retrospect.","note":{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"\"Bibliographical note\": p. 173-175."},"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-uk---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Churchill, Winston",{"@type":"date","#text":"1874-1965"}]}},{"@authority":"fast","temporal":"1900-1999"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Prime ministers","geographic":"Great Britain"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Great Britain","topic":"Politics and government","temporal":"20th century"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"DA566.9.C5 G44"},"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Great lives observed"}},{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Churchill"},"name":{"namePart":"Gilbert, Martin, 1936-2015."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"Englewood Cliffs, N.J. : Prentice-Hall, [1967]"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)560072690"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990012971850203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^67028397^//r69"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"400983"}],"location"